{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "_about": [
    "Company to assessment mapping, so that '/sim <company>' launches something",
    "sensible. JSON rather than YAML because the engine is stdlib only.",
    "",
    "Every entry MUST carry sources and last_confirmed, and tools/qa.py rejects",
    "entries without them. A preset is a factual claim about what a company",
    "currently does to candidates and people plan their preparation around it.",
    "",
    "TWO SEPARATE CLAIMS, deliberately kept apart:",
    "",
    "  confidence         how sure we are the company uses CodeSignal at all",
    "  format_confidence  how sure we are WHICH assessment they give",
    "",
    "They are not the same and conflating them is how a guess becomes received",
    "wisdom. CodeSignal publishes its customer list, so the first claim is often",
    "solid. It publishes nothing about which format any customer chooses, so the",
    "second is usually unknown and most entries below say so with a null format.",
    "An entry with no format still helps: it tells you the platform, and the",
    "skill then asks which format you want rather than guessing for you.",
    "",
    "confidence and format_confidence:",
    "  high    first-party, or several independent recent reports",
    "  medium  reported, but thinly or not recently",
    "",
    "Formats change every hiring cycle. Your actual invite email names the",
    "platform and the format, and it beats this table every time."
  ],
  "presets": {
    "capital-one": {
      "format": "gca",
      "questions": 4,
      "minutes": 70,
      "confidence": "high",
      "format_confidence": "medium",
      "sources": [
        "https://codesignal.com/customers/",
        "https://github.com/Leader-board/OA-and-Interviews/blob/main/Online%20Assessments.md"
      ],
